  "notes": [
    "Outcome-blind max-terminal-ELO selection audit PASS; archived iteration2 checkpoint and terminal snapshot id2 model states are bit-identical.",
    "All four treatment raw pair streams hash-validated and aligned exactly to the parent terminal-control decks."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "The outcome-blind top ELO survivor was bit-identical across archive and terminal pool evidence and behaviorally differed from the terminal actor, but all four breadth estimates were negative. Its paired pooled delta versus terminal was -51.3027 bb/100 (95% CI [-88.1160,-14.4895]).",
    "conclusion": "Terminal-actor deployment was not the cause of the fresh-zero curriculum failure. Historical snapshot id2 improved the point estimate against the in-training Standard10 anchor without significance, while significantly degrading against every untouched fresh-zero learned anchor. Terminal ELO ratings are exploitative/in-family and not a general-strength selector at this scale.",
    "decision": "REJECT_HISTORICAL_ELO_SURVIVOR_DEPLOYMENT",
    "next_step": "Stop fresh-zero PPO/ELO hyperparameter and selection variants. Design the smallest experiment where heldout cross-play or tournament utility directly changes learned weights, rather than only choosing opponents or a checkpoint; preserve Standard10 as a reference while avoiding imitation-only and average-policy routes already disproven."
  },
